{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And so shall you make</b> — for all generations: if one of the vessels is lost, or when you make vessels for the permanent Temple, such as the tables, menorot, basins, and stands that Solomon made — according to this pattern shall you make them. And if the verse were not connected to what precedes it, it would not have written וְכֵן תַּעֲשׂוּ (\"and so shall you make\"), but rather כֵּן תַּעֲשׂוּ (\"so shall you make\"), and it would have been speaking about the making of the Tent of Meeting and its vessels. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 25:9). But I do not know whether this is correct, that Solomon would be obligated to make vessels for the permanent Temple according to this pattern, seeing that the bronze altar that Solomon made was twenty cubits long and twenty cubits wide (II Chronicles 4:1).\n\nAnd R. Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 25:9) that וְכֵן תַּעֲשׂוּ (\"and so shall you make\") refers to the vessels, since at the beginning He said, \"And they shall make Me a sanctuary.\" But according to the plain sense there is no need for any of this. Rather, the repetition comes for emphasis and exhortation: He said, \"And they shall make Me a sanctuary\" — a house and vessels like the sanctuary of a king and a royal palace (Amos 7:13); \"and I will dwell among them\" — in the house and in the seat of Glory that they make for Me there; \"according to all that I show you, the pattern of the tabernacle\" — this one about which I said that I will dwell in it among them; \"and the pattern of all its vessels.\" And He repeated וְכֵן תַּעֲשׂוּ (\"and so shall you make\") — all of you, with zeal and diligence. And it is like the repetition in \"And the children of Israel did according to all that YHWH commanded Moses, so (כֵּן) they did\" (Exodus 39:32), for since it is a commandment, He said וְכֵן תַּעֲשׂוּ."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:18:43.365998341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}